# D2 1.1 -- who is the infrastructure manager for this line?
#
# Every section of line declares one: era:infrastructureManager points at an
# era:OrganisationRole (.../organisationRole/0080_IM), which era:roleOf
# resolves to the organisation itself. 1,111,592 statements graph-wide, and
# 334 of 334 sections on DEU line 4000 carry it.
#
# Answering this from the named graph instead -- "the Body holding the IM role
# inside the graph that publishes the line" -- looks equivalent and is not.
# Both German bodies sit in both German graphs, so that route names DB InfraGO
# *and* Deutsche Bahn AG for line 4000, where the declared property names
# DB InfraGO alone. The graph is still worth reporting, as the separate fact it
# is: line 4000 is published in two datasets.
#
# Operational points do not carry era:infrastructureManager -- 0 of the 308 on
# DEU line 4000 -- so the section side is the one to ask.
#
# Against rinf-plus. 0.11 s.
PREFIX era: <http://data.europa.eu/949/>
PREFIX eu:  <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/>
SELECT DISTINCT ?body ?code ?graph WHERE {
  GRAPH ?graph { ?sol a era:SectionOfLine ; era:inCountry eu:DEU ; era:nationalLine/era:lineId "4000" ;
                      era:infrastructureManager ?role }
  ?role era:roleOf ?body .
  ?body era:organisationCode ?code .
}
ORDER BY ?code
